{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790994740,"nonce":"AaNJp60xGGNsgOLq8hXUuLXCNx4=","title":"Colour transitions lagged behind hover and scheme changes in a window","message":"Measured with a window harness (WindowedApp, a button with bg-primary hover:bg-primary-hover transition-colors, timing every presented frame):\n\n- A scheme switch: the page background settled in about 275 ms, but the transitioned button trailed it and was still moving at 700 ms. The scheme spring moves every themed colour each frame, and each move restarted the button's 180 ms tween from where it was, so it chased the theme.\n- A change made by code rather than by a window event (onFrame, a watch, a timer) waited for the loop's idle timeout, up to 100 ms, before the next frame.\n- Watches that Blinc queued during its own flush reacted only at the next flush.\n\nFixed: a tween follows its value directly while a scheme transition runs (the theme already animates it); the loop polls instead of waiting when a frame is due; LayoutTree.flush drains watches queued during Blinc's flush. After: hover's first frame lands 9 ms after the event, and a transitioned button moves in step with the page through a scheme switch, both settling by about 267 ms.\n\nThe smoke check added with this (\"keeps up with a scheme transition\") pins the fixed behaviour but passes on the old code too in the smoke harness, where the tween did not trail; the window harness is what showed the lag.","files":null}]}